<title>NETHERLANDS: Schiphol September airfreight rises 8.9pct.</title>
<headline>Schiphol September airfreight rises 8.9pct.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amsterdam Schiphol airport handled 8.9 percent more airfreight in September, the airport's operating company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Schiphol's statistics department said the airport handled 87,162 tonnes of airfreight last month.</p>
<p>Provisional figures for last month showed a sharp rise in air transport movements, climbing 13.3 per cent to a total of 28,351 movements, with most growth reported on short- haul European feeder routes.</p>
<p>The airport said the charter market remains weak, but there was strong growth in the number of transfer passengers using the leading Dutch airport, up 15 percent over this time last year, Schiphol said.</p>
<p>		   Sept 1996    96 vs 95    Jan-Sept 96   96 vs 95</p>
<p>Movements	   28,351     13.3pct    240,375	  10.3pct</p>
<p>Passengers(million)2.64	9.3pct     20.66	     8.9pct</p>
<p>Freight(tonnes)   87,162	8.9pct     781,575	 11.0pct</p>
<p>Source: Amsterdam Airport Schiphol.  NB: All figures are</p>
<p>provisional.</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
